[system]
You are a demanding fiction editor. Every finding must point at exact words in the scene.
[user]
SCENE TEXT
"""{{ text }}"""

List up to {{ max_findings }} concrete weaknesses in this scene.
For each finding:
- "quote": copy 8–30 words exactly as they appear in the scene (same punctuation).
- "problem": in your own words, what is wrong with that passage. Do NOT repeat the quote.
- "suggestion": one specific change that would fix it.
- "category" and "severity" from the allowed values.

Example of the expected shape (different scene):
{"findings": [{"quote": "The wind howled like a wolf in the dark night", "category": "prose", "severity": "low",
  "problem": "Stock simile; the image adds nothing specific to this coast.", "suggestion": "Replace with a concrete detail, e.g. the shutters' rhythm against the frame."}]}
